  "description": "The configuration titled **Device Data Export** (name) belongs to organization\u202f5f2d1c3a9b8e4f6a7b0c1d2e (orgId) and uses the application template\u202fa1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c (applicationTemplateId). It is intended to export device data and events to cloud storage, as described: \u201cConfiguration for exporting device data and events to cloud storage.\u201d The public endpoint will be accessible via the slug **my\u2011endpoint\u201101**, with CORS enabled by default. User tokens will be considered expired after **2025\u201112\u201131\u202f23:59:59\u202fUTC**, and a blob URL time\u2011to\u2011live of 86\u202f400\u202fseconds (24\u202fhours) is specified. Two global variables are defined: an API key (**key**\u202f=\u202fapiKey) with JSON value `{\"value\":\"12345-abcde\"}`, not limited to the cloud (cloudOnly\u202f=\u202ffalse) and described as \u201cAPI key used for external services,\u201d and a feature flag (**key**\u202f=\u202ffeatureFlag) with JSON value `{\"enabled\":true}` described as \u201cToggle for new feature rollout.\u201d\n\nThe archive settings place files under the directory **archives/2025**, operating in **whitelist** mode. Only the devices with IDs **a1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c** and **d4e5f60718293a4b5ca1b2c3** are included, and devices tagged **environment=production** are also selected. The configuration includes devices (includeDevices\u202f=\u202ftrue) but excludes events (includeEvents\u202f=\u202ffalse) while including data tables (includeDataTables\u202f=\u202ftrue). Data tables are handled in **blacklist** mode, with the table ID **f60718293a4b5ca1b2c3d4e5** explicitly excluded. Archive files are stored in Amazon S3 using bucket **my-archive-bucket**, access key ID **AKIAEXAMPLEKEY**, secret access key **wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY**, and region **us\u2011west\u20112**."
